{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia","id":1442755,"title":"[Aberrant] I don't trust Project Utopia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-05T12:42:45-07:00","id":1442755,"title":"[Aberrant] I don't trust Project Utopia","content":"I just don't trust Project Utopia. There's just gotta be something up with them. Am I justified in my distrust, or do I have too much 1E on the brain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T12:57:45-07:00","id":1442759,"title":"","content":"You have too much 1e. They intentionally made Project Utopia less nefarious. Now, they do still have Proteus' Medusa Protocols, but they're not sterilizing novas or anything like that in this version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T13:00:29-07:00","id":1442760,"title":"","content":"Probably too much 1st edition. Even in 1st edition Utopia was largely run by good people. Proteus in an effort to control nova growth overstepped the boundaries of their operation. I suspect Max Mercer dealt with it at some point. Hope, Faith, Unity ate good ideals to aspire to. Utopia as an child pf the Aeon Society tries to live up to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T13:13:49-07:00","id":1442762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomeborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia#post1442755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't trust Project Utopia. There's just gotta be something up with them. Am I justified in my distrust, or do I have too much 1E on the brain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any organization, Utopia probably has a few bad eggs, or has made some well-intentioned missteps, but on the whole Utopia is a force for good. We intentionally avoided the secret conspiracy angle this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T13:51:59-07:00","id":1442765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia?p=1442762#post1442762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like any organization, Utopia probably has a few bad eggs, or has made some well-intentioned missteps, but on the whole Utopia is a force for good. We intentionally avoided the secret conspiracy angle this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess I just read the book (I know I'm late) and just got this &quot;too good to be true&quot; vibes from them. Maybe I'm just too cynical, which would make me fit right in with the politicians in the United States. Not a good look for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T16:30:35-07:00","id":1442781,"title":"","content":"In my game Utopia has the best intentions and try to promote social projects and help communities in need. While they have Protheus, Thetis and the Babel Dossier, they still do not with the best intentions.<br /> <br /> Even Protheus is not made by a bunch of paranoid sociopaths, they are, yes, paranoids, but they are not hunting novas to test on them, they just watch the training and tests the novas do in the utopia facilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T20:00:01-07:00","id":1442796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomeborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia?p=1442765#post1442765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just read the book (I know I'm late) and just got this &quot;too good to be true&quot; vibes from them. Maybe I'm just too cynical, which would make me fit right in with the politicians in the United States. Not a good look for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could argue that the &quot;too good to be true&quot; vibe is a result of the various Aeon groups being subtly overseen by a literal time traveler who also happens to be the luckiest man alive. Of course they come off as impossibly good; Mercer knows all sorts of ways that things could go wrong, and has preemptively put into place procedures and personnel choices that make those outcomes much less likely, and may have all sorts of super advanced talent Gifts related to effectively running large organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T20:30:53-07:00","id":1442799,"title":"","content":"Thankfully they are the good guys. I had a problem with the dark conspiracy angle in 1e. It was fun and made for some good story ideas but way to many novas running around with enhanced senses, telepathy, bio manipulation, mega-int and much more to ever allow a conspiracy like that to stay hidden. <br /> I know a lot would be over looked as people just don\u2019t want to believe their saviors are the bad guys. However that would only go so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T00:04:15-07:00","id":1442807,"title":"","content":"It would require a lot of effort and very clever plotting, but if you really want to grim it up, make the story of Utopia how an organization of good, motivated, thoughtful people still manage to have their efforts lead to monstrous outcomes despite never falling to the dark side. <br /> <br /> Your players may or may not like the implicit moral that the world is inevitably bad and going to hell, and that adding superpowers just turns up the heat on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T00:51:22-07:00","id":1442809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia?p=1442796#post1442796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could argue that the &quot;too good to be true&quot; vibe is a result of the various Aeon groups being subtly overseen by a literal time traveler who also happens to be the luckiest man alive. Of course they come off as impossibly good; Mercer knows all sorts of ways that things could go wrong, and has preemptively put into place procedures and personnel choices that make those outcomes much less likely, and may have all sorts of super advanced talent Gifts related to effectively running large organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mercer has less influence over Utopia than you might think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T07:34:15-07:00","id":1442836,"title":"","content":"Do not have <b>Aberrant</b>, but seen Mercer name mentioned in here - <b>So can someone quickly sum-up me what is Project Utopia in <i>Aberrant</i>?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-06-2021, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T08:39:05-07:00","id":1442842,"title":"","content":"Utopia is the project in Aeon society that used to study Stalwarts (there is one for Mesmerists, one for Daredevils and one for strange places and creatures). When the novas show up after N-Day, Aeon \u201cempower\u201d project Utopia and they start to train and help Novas to achieve their potential. At same time they start using this novas to help the world, fighting organized crime, world hunger, fixing global warming, etc. they also bring up the equivalent of Justice League, Team Tomorrow (T2M)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T12:02:59-07:00","id":1442864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia?p=1442836#post1442836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not have <b>Aberrant</b>, but seen Mercer name mentioned in here - <b>So can someone quickly sum-up me what is Project Utopia in <i>Aberrant</i>?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Content is 1e but: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Utopia\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Utopia</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T13:06:13-07:00","id":1442871,"title":"","content":"In simplest terms it\u2019s an NGO dedicated to helping train Novas and working with world governments to employ the Novas they train to use their abilities toward the betterment of the world (or at least betterment as defined by the elites of the governments they work with). They also work with law enforcement agencies to lend Nova support when needed to act against Nova criminals that baseline law enforcement can\u2019t handle.<br /> <br /> As you might imagine, Divis Mal (Michael)\u2018s faction, Teragen think this is all ways to keep Novas in line and beholden to baselines instead of reaching their full transcendent potential.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s at least one NPC though, Antaeus (think Swamp Thing), who is a member of Project Utopia working on environmental projects, while also pursuing the philosophy of Teras with regard to his own evolution - which makes everybody nervous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-06-2021, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T09:34:06-07:00","id":1442982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1442755-aberrant-i-don-t-trust-project-utopia?p=1442871#post1442871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In simplest terms it\u2019s an NGO dedicated to helping train Novas and working with world governments to employ the Novas they train to use their abilities toward the betterment of the world (or at least betterment as defined by the elites of the governments they work with). They also work with law enforcement agencies to lend Nova support when needed to act against Nova criminals that baseline law enforcement can\u2019t handle.<br /> <br /> As you might imagine, Divis Mal (Michael)\u2018s faction, Teragen think this is all ways to keep Novas in line and beholden to baselines instead of reaching their full transcendent potential.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s at least one NPC though, Antaeus (think Swamp Thing), who is a member of Project Utopia working on environmental projects, while also pursuing the philosophy of Teras with regard to his own evolution - which makes everybody nervous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this is a fair description that allows for personal value level assessment (in character or otherwise) of Utopia's relative goodness.<br /> <br /> Some people may see some aspects as &quot;too good to be true&quot; because we have so few unadulterated organizations like that in our current real world. I think that may be for lack of trying than any actual human limitation.<br /> <br /> Even if it isn't secretly nefarious, to some people it is openly problematic. They aren't necessarily my personal real world views, but today's force for good given power can become tomorrow's force for greed and oppression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}